() Tj
T*
(HMETIS-REFINEMENT AND NATURAL HIERARCHICAL GRAPH NOTES) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Main Research Story) Tj
T*
(----------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The current project direction is:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> Use hMETIS as a structure-aware refinement tool for the Maximum Coverage Problem) Tj
T*
(> on hierarchical community-structured hypergraphs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The claim is not that hMETIS universally beats greedy. The more accurate claim is:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> On graphs with community and subcommunity overlap structure, hMETIS-refinement) Tj
T*
(> can improve greedy by finding structurally diverse replacement candidates.) Tj
T*
(> Tabu search still gives the best final quality, but hMETIS-refinement captures) Tj
T*
(> part of tabu's improvement with lower runtime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Natural Hierarchical Graph) Tj
T*
(-----------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The graph is generated in `experiment_natural_hierarchy.py`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The vertices are grouped into hidden communities and subcommunities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(community) Tj
T*
(  subcommunity) Tj
T*
(    vertices) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For example, in the large setting:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(nvtxs = 4800) Tj
T*
(n_communities = 12) Tj
T*
(subcommunities_per_community = 5) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This means:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12 communities) Tj
T*
(5 subcommunities in each community) Tj
T*
(60 total subcommunities) Tj
T*
(about 400 vertices per community) Tj
T*
(about 80 vertices per subcommunity) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Communities and subcommunities are hidden generation labels. They are not) Tj
T*
(selectable edges and they do not directly cover anything.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. What Communities Are Used For) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Communities and subcommunities are only sampling pools.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
