(community labels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. hMETIS-Refinement Algorithm) Tj
T*
(------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(hMETIS-refinement uses hMETIS as a candidate generator, not as the final solver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It has two phases.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Phase 1: hMETIS Candidate-Pool Construction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(start with empty selected set) Tj
T*
(while budget is not full:) Tj
T*
(    write current residual hypergraph to hMETIS) Tj
T*
(    partition remaining candidate edges) Tj
T*
(    take top candidates from each partition) Tj
T*
(    choose globally using current marginal coverage gain) Tj
T*
(    update selected edges and covered vertices) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is not simply "pick one edge from every partition." The partition only) Tj
T*
(creates a diversified candidate pool. Marginal coverage still decides selection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Phase 2: hMETIS-Guided Swap Refinement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After the initial solution is full:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(repeat for several rounds:) Tj
T*
(    run hMETIS again) Tj
T*
(    collect replacement candidates from partitions) Tj
T*
(    for each candidate edge not currently selected:) Tj
T*
(      for each selected edge:) Tj
T*
(      compute exact coverage change if swapped) Tj
T*
(    accept the best positive-gain swap) Tj
T*
(    stop when no positive-gain swap exists) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The most important rule:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(accept a swap only if actual MCP coverage improves) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(So hMETIS proposes candidates, but the MCP objective makes the final decision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Why Refinement Is More Reliable Than Direct hMETIS Selection) Tj
T*
(----------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The original direct hMETIS method tries to use partitions too directly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That can fail because:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(hMETIS minimizes cuts; MCP maximizes covered vertices) Tj
T*
(partition-local choice may ignore global marginal gain) Tj
T*
(early mistakes cannot be repaired) Tj
T*
(one-per-partition constraints can reject good choices) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
