() Tj
T*
(hMETIS-refinement is safer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(hMETIS only proposes candidates) Tj
T*
(coverage gain accepts or rejects each swap) Tj
T*
(bad hMETIS suggestions are ignored) Tj
T*
(earlier selected edges can be replaced) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Difference From Tabu) Tj
T*
(------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tabu is a broader local search:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(starts from greedy) Tj
T*
(tries many possible swaps) Tj
T*
(can accept non-improving moves) Tj
T*
(uses memory to avoid cycling) Tj
T*
(keeps the best solution found) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(hMETIS-refinement is narrower:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(starts from hMETIS candidate-pool solution) Tj
T*
(uses hMETIS partitions to propose replacement candidates) Tj
T*
(accepts only improving swaps) Tj
T*
(does not accept worse moves) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Therefore tabu usually has better final quality, but hMETIS-refinement is faster) Tj
T*
(and more directly tied to the hypergraph partitioning idea.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. hMETIS Parameters) Tj
T*
(---------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The main hMETIS-refinement configuration is:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(nparts = 16) Tj
T*
(top_per_partition = 4) Tj
T*
(min_gain_ratio = 0.70) Tj
T*
(refine_top_per_partition = 10) Tj
T*
(refine_rounds = 5) Tj
T*
(timeout = 45 seconds) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### nparts = 16) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This means hMETIS partitions the candidate edge-space into 16 parts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why 16?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(small enough to keep runtime manageable) Tj
T*
(large enough to expose multiple communities/subcommunities) Tj
T*
(stable across small, medium, and large tests) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Using too few partitions gives weak diversity. Using too many partitions) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
