stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 760 Td
14 TL
(increases runtime and may make partitions too small/noisy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For larger future tests, `nparts = 32` is worth trying, but for the current) Tj
T*
(focused comparison `p16` is the clean default.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### top_per_partition = 4) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(During construction, each partition contributes up to 4 candidate edges.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why 4?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1 candidate per partition is too restrictive) Tj
T*
(too many candidates makes hMETIS guidance less meaningful) Tj
T*
(4 keeps a small but flexible candidate pool) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### min_gain_ratio = 0.70) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A candidate must have at least 70% of the current global best marginal gain to) Tj
T*
(be considered during construction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(prevents selecting very weak edges just for diversity) Tj
T*
(still allows hMETIS to choose slightly less greedy but more diverse edges) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### refine_top_per_partition = 10) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(During refinement, each partition can contribute up to 10 replacement candidates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why more than construction?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(refinement needs a broader pool to find useful swaps) Tj
T*
(bad candidates are safe because swaps must improve actual coverage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### refine_rounds = 5) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The algorithm repeats hMETIS-guided swap search for up to 5 rounds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why 5?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(enough to find multiple improvements) Tj
T*
(avoids very long runtimes) Tj
T*
(usually stops early if no improving swaps exist) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### timeout = 45 seconds) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each hMETIS call has a timeout to avoid hanging on larger instances.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13. Current Comparison Result) Tj
T*
(-----------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
